/S /H1
/P 110 0 R
/T (ABSTRACT)
/E (ABSTRACT)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (            Employee attrition presents a workforce planning challenge because historical employee records contain many interacting factors that may be associated with departure. WorkforceIQ is an educational machine learning and workforce analytics system designed to explore these associations and demonstrate an end-to-end prediction workflow. The project uses the fictional IBM HR Analytics Employee Attrition dataset, containing 1,470 records and 35 original columns. Four non-informative or identifier columns were removed, leaving 30 input features. Categorical encoding and numerical scaling were integrated with model training in a Scikit-learn pipeline. An 80:20 stratified split and five-fold stratified cross-validation supported model comparison.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (          Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest and XGBoost were compared. Logistic Regression was selected for its average precision and minority-class recall in the initial comparison. A decision threshold of 0.75 was selected using training out-of-fold F1 scores. On the test set, the selected threshold produced 85.03% accuracy, 54.29% precision, 40.43% recall and 46.34% F1. ROC-AUC was 0.8032 and average precision was 0.5612. The threshold reduces false alarms but misses more attrition cases than the default threshold.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (          The system combines a React analytics interface with a FastAPI REST backend and a serialized model. The frontend and backend were deployed using Netlify and Render respectively. The initial verified test run recorded 48 passing automated tests. The project demonstrates data analysis, model evaluation, API integration and deployment. Its fictional dataset, uncalibrated scores and previously inspected test set limit real-world applicability. The system is not intended for employment decisions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
